S4. G2's NUMERICAL REPRODUCIBILITY under a domain-decomposition change
================================================================================================
  W4-defect-reach/run_cbfs_arm.sh copies 0/, constant/, system/ and runScript.py from
  W4-adjoint-pc-unblock/cbfs_beta and changes ONE thing: decomposeParDict to simple [4,1,1].
  Same image, same DAFOAM_SUBPC_TYPE=lu, np=4, beta == 1, same objective. Pure numerics.

  THE ORDERING TRAP, EXHIBITED FIRST. DV order follows the decomposition, so the two
  arrays are in DIFFERENT DV orders and are a permutation of one another:
    max |sorted(|A|) - sorted(|B|)|  = 7.269e-10   (they hold the same values)
    UNPERMUTED Spearman(|A|,|B|)     = +0.0901  and G2 would read 31.1905% vs 14.0952%
    A 17-point 'finding' is available to anyone who skips the permutation.

  POSITIVE CONTROL on the addressing parser: the map built here for arm A is
    identical to the archived dv_to_serial_perm.npy, entry for entry: True
    per-rank cell counts  A [5254, 5204, 5262, 5280]   B [5250, 5250, 5250, 5250]

  PERMUTED, in serial cell order:
    ||A-B|| / ||A||                 = 1.132e-04  (record publishes 1.13e-04)
    top-20 |g| cells: max rel 1.582e-04, median rel 3.955e-05  (record publishes 1.58e-04, 4.0e-05)
    Spearman(|A|,|B|) = +0.99999988

    G2  arm A (scotch)        = 31.1905%   (R1 publishes 31.19% for this array)
    G2  arm B (simple 4x1x1)  = 31.1905%
    DELTA under a lever with no physics in it = +0.0000 percentage points
    top-decile set agreement = 2100 of 2100 cells = 100.00%

================================================================================================
S5. G-P2's STATED MECHANISM, at the one state where it can be checked
================================================================================================
  G-P2 (S1_PRIORS_PREREGISTRATION.md S4) predicts before any compute:
    'the restoring pull at beta = 0.2 is 2*lambda_LN*log(0.2)/0.2 = 1.309e-4 against the
     Gaussian's 2*lambda_L2*(0.2-1) = 1.600e-5 -- 8.2x stronger. Prediction: the count of
     cells at the lower bound falls from 223 to fewer than 60.'
  Whether a cell unpins is not decided by prior-vs-prior. It is decided by prior pull versus
  LIKELIHOOD pull at that cell, and the likelihood pull is on disk at evaluation 10.

    lognormal pull at beta=0.2 (lambda_LN 8.1335e-06) = 1.3090e-04
    Gaussian  pull at beta=0.2 (lambda_L2 1e-5)        = 1.6000e-05   ratio 8.18x (prereg 8.2x)

    Cells at the lower bound at evaluation 10: 5 of 21000.
    FRAME, stated not glossed: the FINAL state has 223 low + 1 high, but its gradient
    is deleted by invert_lbfgsb.py:96-97. Evaluation 10 is the only archived state
    where beta and its gradient can both be read, and it is early in the trajectory.

    |g_QoI| at those cells: min 4.6498e-04  p50 6.8796e-04  max 1.8206e-03
    exceeding the lognormal pull 1.3090e-04 : 100.00% (5 of 5)
    exceeding the Gaussian  pull 1.6000e-05 : 100.00% (5 of 5)
    median |g_QoI| at the bound is 5.3x the lognormal restoring pull.

    Reading, bounded by the frame: at every archived pinned cell the likelihood pull already
    exceeds the stronger prior's restoring pull by a factor of several, so the 8.2x prior
    ratio does not by itself imply unpinning. n = 5 is small and the state is not the one
    G-P2 grades; this is a caution on the mechanism, not a measurement of the gate.

DONE.
